      "reasoning": "The two diagonals intersect at O, so AO and OC lie on one line and DO and OB lie on the other. Since AD is parallel to BC, triangles AOD and COB are similar, so AO:OC = DO:OB = 3:5. For part (1), [AOB]/[ODC] = (AO·OB·sin∠AOB)/(OC·OD·sin∠COD) = (AO/OC)(OB/OD) because ∠AOB and ∠COD are vertical. This is (3/5)(5/3)=1, so their areas are equal; both are 12 cm^2. For part (2), triangles ODC and OBC have the same base OC. Their vertices D and B lie on the same line DB through O, so their perpendicular distances to OC are in the ratio OD:OB = 3:5. Thus [ODC]:[OBC]=3:5 and [OBC]=(5/3)·12=20 cm^2."
